  "source_caption": "The Weeknd’s new music video for Hong Kong, directed by Evan Larsen, draws heavily from the visual world of Wong Kar-wai, particularly Chungking Express (1994) and Fallen Angels (1995). From the neon-lit streets to the framing and hazy cityscapes, the parallels are intentional, with Larsen revealing that The Weeknd shared a list of Hong Kong films as inspiration.\n\nThe connection goes a little deeper, too. The song samples Seasonal Wind, a 1993 track by Faye Wong, who also starred in Chungking Express. A fitting tribute to Hong Kong cinema.",
